A||||10||Max The Chainsaw||Automatic Wipers?||||1||
Z||000000||Max The Chainsaw||10-09-2000||08:59 PM||||Hi,<P>I have an unusual problem with the wipers on my 86 2M4. At first they would make one swipe  when I signaled a turn, (Not always, about once a day). I thought there may be a short in the signal switch arm. But now they also do it once in awhile when the car is started.  Could this be a problem in the park switch inside the motor? I sure hate to replace an $80 turn switch arm if that's not the trouble.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||10-09-2000||10:11 PM||||I'm having a similar problem with my 85, the wipers go one swip when I signal and when the signal turns off, it also now started doing it when I flick on my highbeams. I think it's the switch inside the column. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||10-09-2000||10:27 PM||||it seems to be a common GM problem... my friends station wagon does it, both of my fieros have done it, and my other friend's firebird does it.  i've been told that the switch in the column needs to be replaced... i'm too lazy so i hooked up my own switch to the fuse for the wipers just so i wouldn't look dumb on the dry days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-10-2000||09:01 AM||||replace the stalk. The knob end of it goes bad. the problem is not inside the column but you have to take the wheel off to remove it I think. been awhile since I had it apart.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||10-10-2000||10:04 AM||||I had the same problem until I heard some plastic in the column snap.  Problem stopped, but now my washer squirter ended up not working too.  I think it's the switch in the column.  (I could be wrong) either way, the steering wheel has to come off.  I've had that wheel off so many times, I don't feel like fixing it right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> What a pain without the right tools.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||wwh0001||10-10-2000||11:37 AM||||The Phantom wiper swipe is norammly not a result of the turn signal stalk ( easy fix if it is just push in twist and pull out) Most of the time is is the switch in the column or the circuit board in the wiper motor. Both requiring repalcement if malfunctioning. The circuit board is an easy fix, the column switch requires a lot of work and special tools.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||10-10-2000||03:57 PM||||The problem is NOT in the stalk.  The stalk is just a stick that is used to operate the switch which is inside the column.  The only thing the stalk does itself is operate the cruise control.  While it also could be the wiper control module, in several of my Fieros (and an Astro van) it was the wiper switch in the column.<P>I picked up a replacement switch from Advance Auto for about $55.  It is GP Sorensen #DS170.  The switch is a pain to get to but not really difficult, just time consuming.  You need to remove the wheel, lock plate, turn signal stalk, ignition key switch to get to the wiper switch.  Installation is the reverse of removal.  I didn't get the key buzzer contact back in correctly so my key chime doesn't work (no big deal).<P>Good luck....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Max The Chainsaw||10-13-2000||11:23 AM||||Thanks Guys,<P>Guess I gota tear into it after all.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Think I'll let it ride till spring, too much going on right now getting the house ready for winter, (Digging up a leaking sewer pipe...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   ) And I should have a bit more cash for the switches then.<P>Thanks again for all the help.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||10-13-2000||12:25 PM||||I've discovered that mine only does it when it's cool outside. It does it in the morning and late i the evening but not mid after noon. This seems a strange problem. <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||wwh0001||10-13-2000||01:39 PM||||If this happens when it is cool and normally never when warm, then chances are it is the circuit board in the wiper motor.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ka4nkf||10-15-2000||10:36 PM||||I think the problem Is in the wiper motor circut board. the reason I say this is not only does mine swipe one time using the turn signal, It also sometimes swipes one time when I turn the ignition switch on. I dont even have my hand on the turn signal, so I dont see how it could be the switch. but I dont know everything. I am going to change the board in the wiper motor.||||reg||1
